---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import MulchCalculator from '../components/MulchCalculator.astro';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="Mulch Calculator — How Much Mulch Do I Need? | HomeDIYCalcs"
  description="Free mulch calculator. Calculate how many cubic yards or bags of mulch you need for your garden beds, based on area and depth."
>
  <section class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <div class="mb-12 text-center">
      <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl md:text-5xl text-ink mb-4">Mulch Calculator</h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-ink-muted max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        Calculate how much mulch you need in cubic yards and bags. Enter the size of your bed and how deep you want the mulch.
      </p>
    </div>

    <MulchCalculator />

    <div class="mt-16 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-4">How to calculate mulch</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal list-inside text-ink space-y-2 mb-8">
        <li>Measure the length and width of your bed in feet.</li>
        <li>Decide on depth — 2–3 inches is standard for garden beds.</li>
        <li>Volume = length × width × depth (converted to feet).</li>
        <li>Divide by 27 to get cubic yards, since one cubic yard = 27 cubic feet.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-4">How many bags of mulch in a cubic yard?</h2>
      <p class="text-ink-muted mb-8">
        Bagged mulch usually comes in 2 cubic foot bags. Since a cubic yard is 27 cubic feet, that's about 13.5 bags per cubic yard. For larger areas, buying mulch in bulk by the cubic yard is almost always cheaper than bags.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-4">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-medium text-ink mb-2">How deep should mulch be?</h3>
          <p class="text-ink-muted">2–3 inches is ideal for most beds. Too thin won't suppress weeds or hold moisture; too thick (over 4 inches) can suffocate roots and cause rot. Refresh to maintain 2–3 inches each season.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-medium text-ink mb-2">Is it cheaper to buy mulch in bulk or bags?</h3>
          <p class="text-ink-muted">Bulk by the cubic yard is usually much cheaper per volume than bags, but bags are easier to transport and handle for small jobs. For anything over about 2 cubic yards, bulk delivery is normally worth it.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-medium text-ink mb-2">Does this work for soil or gravel too?</h3>
          <p class="text-ink-muted">The volume math is the same for any material spread to a depth — soil, compost, or gravel. Just note that gravel is sold by weight (tons) as well as volume, so check your supplier's units.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-line">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-4">More calculators</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-2">
          <li><a href="/tile-calculator" style="color: var(--color-accent);" class="hover:underline">Tile calculator</a></li>
          <li><a href="/paint-calculator" style="color: var(--color-accent);" class="hover:underline">Paint calculator</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>